---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons doctor -h <==
Diagnose what omaddons manages (bare: diagnose; changes nothing outside its run record)

Usage: omaddons doctor [OPTIONS]
       omaddons doctor <COMMAND>

Commands:
  diagnose  Find what is broken, with evidence and the exact fix (changes nothing outside its run
            record)
  explain   One failure mode in full: what it is, why it matters, and its live instances (changes
            nothing)
  fix       Repair the findings a fixer can repair, as one undoable transaction
  diff      Show what doctor fix would change, or what changed since a run (changes nothing)
  undo      Undo a doctor repair: revert a fix run (or the newest one), strictly
  gc        Delete old doctor runs and what they kept, never what an unfinished change needs

Options:
      --only <IDS>           Only these checks: failure-mode ids or subsystem names, comma-separated
      --skip <IDS>           Not these checks (wins over --only)
      --severity <SEVERITY>  Report findings of this severity and more severe ones only [possible
                             values: P0, P1, P2, P3]
      --quick                Only the fast checks (the cached and quick tiers)
      --include-deep         Also the deep checks
      --online               Also the checks that need the network
      --budget <DURATION>    The whole run's time, shared by the checks by their cost: 500ms or 2s
      --since <RUN>          Compare with an earlier run: its id, or latest

Examples:
  omaddons doctor                what is broken, with evidence and the fix
  omaddons doctor explain fm-configs-config-parse-error
                                 one failure mode in full
  omaddons doctor fix --dry-run  what a repair would change

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons doctor --help <==
Diagnose what omaddons manages (bare: diagnose; changes nothing outside its run record)

Usage: omaddons doctor [OPTIONS]
       omaddons doctor <COMMAND>

Commands:
  diagnose  Find what is broken, with evidence and the exact fix (changes nothing outside its run
            record)
  explain   One failure mode in full: what it is, why it matters, and its live instances (changes
            nothing)
  fix       Repair the findings a fixer can repair, as one undoable transaction
  diff      Show what doctor fix would change, or what changed since a run (changes nothing)
  undo      Undo a doctor repair: revert a fix run (or the newest one), strictly
  gc        Delete old doctor runs and what they kept, never what an unfinished change needs

Options:
      --only <IDS>
          Only these checks: failure-mode ids or subsystem names, comma-separated

      --skip <IDS>
          Not these checks (wins over --only)

      --severity <SEVERITY>
          Report findings of this severity and more severe ones only
          
          [possible values: P0, P1, P2, P3]

      --quick
          Only the fast checks (the cached and quick tiers)

      --include-deep
          Also the deep checks

      --online
          Also the checks that need the network

      --budget <DURATION>
          The whole run's time, shared by the checks by their cost: 500ms or 2s

      --since <RUN>
          Compare with an earlier run: its id, or latest

Examples:
  omaddons doctor                         every check but the deep ones
  omaddons doctor --quick                 the fast checks only
  omaddons doctor --only fm-userland_state-target-vanished
                                          one check
  omaddons doctor --since latest          what changed since the last run
  omaddons doctor explain fm-userland_state-target-vanished
                                          one failure mode in full
  omaddons doctor fix --dry-run           what a repair would change
  omaddons doctor fix --if-match <token>  that repair, exactly as previewed

The doctor exits with its own codes:
  0   healthy                 every selected check ran to completion and found
                              nothing
  1   findings_present        the run completed and reports findings, a check
                              that could not finish among them
  2   fix_partial             a fix ran and some findings remain
  3   fix_failed_rolled_back  a fix failed and was rolled back; nothing changed
  4   refused_unsafe          refused before changing anything: a safety
                              precondition, a missing --force, a conflict, a
                              stale preview or an over-budget selection
  5   concurrency_lost        another omaddons process held the lock past the
                              acquire timeout
  6   online_required         the selection needs the network: add --online
  64  usage_error             unknown command or flag, or a bad argument
  66  no_input                a target, run, failure mode or other input was
                              not found, or is ambiguous
  73  cannot_create           the run directory could not be created
  74  io_error                a runtime failure: I/O, state, network or
                              internal

See also: doctor explain, doctor fix, status

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the
                         Classic Era client), family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every
                         client) [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change
                         nothing)
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by
                         commands that change nothing)
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
